---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Contact: start a conversation with Circulation Studio"
description: "A deliberately small Laguna Beach studio. Tell us about the business and you will hear back from one of us, not a queue."
permalink: /contact/index.html
schemaType: ContactPage
headline: If the timing and fit are right, let’s talk.
lede: We keep the roster small so senior people do the work.
note: >-
  Tell us a little about the business and what you’re after; you’ll hear back
  from one of us, not a queue.
fields:
  - id: name
    label: Name
    type: text
  - id: email
    label: Email
    type: email

# Direction B. Four rows is the ceiling: a fifth turns a light touch into a
# checklist, which is why the listing became a field rather than a fifth prompt.
# Timeline is read for too and changes nothing on screen.
promptsIntro: Recommended topics to cover so we can provide a better answer
prompts:
  - id: what
    label: What you do
    hint: The trade or practice, so we know the category we would be competing in.
  - id: where
    label: Where you are
    hint: City or service area. Local results differ street by street.
  - id: want
    label: What you are after
    hint: More calls, a new site, better reviews, or something you cannot name yet.
  - id: money
    label: Roughly what you have to spend
    hint: >-
      A range in a sentence is plenty. It decides whether the honest answer is us
      or someone else.
---
{#
  Contact.

  NAP renders from site.nap, the single source, so it matches the colophon byte
  for byte. Nothing here is retyped. SCHEMA.md marks this page as the eventual
  home of the LocalBusiness/Organization JSON-LD, which will read the same
  object; no schema is written yet, by instruction.

  AVAILABILITY renders from site.booking, the same source the masthead reads,
  so the two can never state different things. The handoff had the masthead
  saying "Now booking Q3" while this page's prose said "Booking for Q3 is
  open", which is two claims to keep in sync by hand. The prose sentence now
  stops after the roster line and the availability is its own single-sourced
  element.

  EMAIL is obfuscated: no contiguous address and no mailto: in the markup. See
  components/email.njk for how, and the note below on the remaining exposure.

  FORM is a static mockup this pass. No action, no backend. main.js blocks the
  submit so a click cannot silently reload the page and look like a failure.
  Labels are explicit with for/id rather than wrapping, which is better for
  assistive tech than the implicit labels in the handoff.

  One deep ink pane per view: the colophon is it. Nothing on this page adds a
  second.
#}
{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}
{% from "components/section.njk" import section %}
{% from "components/button.njk" import button %}
{% from "components/email.njk" import email %}

{% call container(class="pt-24 pb-16") %}
  <h1 class="cs-contact__headline">{{ headline }}</h1>
  <p class="cs-contact__lede">{{ lede }}</p>
  <p class="cs-contact__availability">{{ site.booking.label }}</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call container(class="pb-24") %}
  <div class="cs-contact__grid">
    <form class="cs-form cs-contact__panel" data-form-mockup>
      <div class="cs-form__row">
        {% for field in fields %}
          <p class="cs-field m-0">
            <label class="cs-field__label" for="field-{{ field.id }}">{{ field.label }}</label>
            <input class="cs-input" type="{{ field.type }}" id="field-{{ field.id }}" name="{{ field.id }}" autocomplete="{{ "name" if field.id == "name" else "email" }}">
          </p>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {#- The listing REPLACED Company / business, per direction B. People paste
          these, and it is the fastest thing anyone can give us: we can read the
          listing before replying. Deliberately not validated beyond type=url's
          own check, because a failed check on a correct paste is worse than no
          check at all. -#}
      <p class="cs-field m-0">
        <label class="cs-field__label" for="field-listing">
          Website or Yelp listing <span class="cs-field__optional">· Optional</span>
        </label>
        <input class="cs-input" type="url" id="field-listing" name="listing"
               autocomplete="url" placeholder="yourbusiness.com, or the Yelp page">
      </p>

      <p class="cs-field m-0">
        <label class="cs-field__label" for="field-message">What are you looking for?</label>
        {#- rows 3, down from 5. At 5 the control read as an empty box even
            once the box was gone, because the empty space was the loudest
            thing in the form. The grip is killed in form.css. -#}
        <textarea class="cs-input" id="field-message" name="message" rows="3"
                  aria-describedby="prompts-intro" data-prompts-source></textarea>
      </p>

      {#- THE PROMPTS. Four rows that light as the message is typed, matched
          entirely in the browser. No request is made, nothing is sent before
          submit, and the submit is NEVER GATED: there is no disabled state, no
          count, no threshold. Send it with all four unlit and the form works
          exactly the same.

          The ticks are aria-hidden and the state is visual only. A screen
          reader gets the guidance line and the four topics, which is the part
          that carries meaning; the lit state is redundant feedback on a thing
          that gates nothing. Announcing it would mean a live region firing on
          every keystroke.

          aria-describedby ties the group's line to the textarea, so the
          guidance is reachable from the field it describes rather than only
          from reading order. -#}
      <div class="cs-prompts" data-prompts>
        <p class="cs-prompts__intro" id="prompts-intro">{{ promptsIntro }}</p>
        <ul class="cs-prompts__list">
          {%- for prompt in prompts %}
          <li class="cs-prompt" data-prompt="{{ prompt.id }}">
            <span class="cs-prompt__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>
              <span class="cs-prompt__label">{{ prompt.label }}</span>
              <span class="cs-prompt__hint">{{ prompt.hint }}</span>
            </span>
          </li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>{{ button("Start the conversation", type="submit") }}</div>
    </form>

    <div class="cs-contact__panel cs-contact__aside">
      <p class="cs-eyebrow">The studio</p>
      {# Single NAP source. Matches the colophon exactly; never retyped. #}
      <address class="cs-contact__nap">
        {{ site.nap.streetAddress }}<br>
        {{ site.nap.cityStateZip }}<br>
        <a href="{{ site.nap.telephoneHref }}">{{ site.nap.telephone }}</a><br>
        {{ email(site.nap.emailUser, site.nap.emailDomain) }}
      </address>
      <p class="cs-contact__note">{{ note }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endcall %}

<div class="cs-sowing">
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--sowing cs-rule--sowing-l" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--sowing cs-rule--sowing-r" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {% call container() %}
    <img class="cs-sowing__figure"
         src="{{ site.cdn }}cs-img-sowing-landscape.webp"
         alt="A hand placing a seed into soil, the deliberate start"
         width="1120" height="520" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
  {% endcall %}
</div>

<div class="pb-24" aria-hidden="true"></div>
